class_name Campaign
extends RefCounted
## All story and scenario content: the intro, the ten fixed chapters (Objective 4) and the good ending.
## One work week: office chapters (1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 9) take turns with off-the-clock chapters at home (3, 5) and in a
## cafe (8, 10), played on the player's phone. Each chapter is a scripted stretch of several items of the SAME attack
## type (TASKS-SPEC.md, sections A and B; docs/PH-CHAPTERS-SCRIPT.md for chapters 3, 5, 8 and 10).
## Every name, domain and number is a fictional placeholder (1326, the real anti-scam hotline, is the exception).
## Item ids keep their original numbers (c3_* lives in Ch4, c8_* in Ch3, ...): ids are opaque.
##
## Chapter keys (A.1):
##   id (its position, 1-10), key (stable slug: email, smishing, ewallet, vishing, bank_agent, bec, social, sideline,
##   qr, identity), title, place ("office", "home" or "cafe"), when (title-card day and time, e.g. "Mon 07:30 PM"),
##   attack (Chapter Select label), music ("day", "drive" or "night"), mood (lighting id of the place's builder),
##   device ("workstation" or "telephone" in the office: where the chapter's first item lives; "phone" at home and in
##   the cafe), app (main channel: "mail", "messages", "chat" or "call"), hint_level ("full", "generic" or "none": the
##   gate hint, difficulty ramp), briefing (Array of {speaker, text}), objective (HUD text at start), items (Array of
##   item dictionaries), debrief, warning_signs, tip, bad_ending (all about the chapter's main attack).
##   Home and cafe chapters only:
##     breach_title (game-over heading, a personal loss; office chapters omit it and keep the Aegis heading),
##     wallet {balance (starting balance as text), base_balance (float; the KwartaPay balance shown = base_balance
##       plus the value of every unlocked item's wallet_tx), history (Array of baseline rows {dir ("in" or "out"),
##       amount, name, number, contact, time, ref}, newest first), inbox (Array of {title, body, time}: official,
##       harmless KwartaPay notices; never a promo that matches a scam)}.
## Item keys (A.2):
##   id (unique campaign-wide), role ("genuine", "fake", "main" or "coworker"), kind ("email", "sms", "chat",
##   "call", "coworker" or "app"), app ("mail", "messages", "chat", "call" or "bank"), task (neutral HUD label, no
##   quote characters), unlock_after (item ids that must be resolved first), required_inspections (gate on the item's
##   step 0), message (email / sms / chat / coworker / app) or call, steps,
##   optional bad_ending, warning_signs, tip (game-over overrides for an unsafe choice in this item),
##   optional extra_inspections (keys required on top of the derived ones: "wallet_inbox" or "page:<PAGES id>"),
##   optional helper_label ("Family" or "Friend": the feedback label of a home or cafe role "coworker" item),
##   optional trap ("mule": a money-mule trap, judged by the Not Your Mule achievement).
##   required_inspections == the derived keys (app mail -> sender, messages -> sender_number, call -> caller_id,
##   chat -> profile, bank -> app_info; kind coworker -> quote; message.request -> request; link:<id> per
##   message.links; qr:<id> per message.qrs; tx:<id> per message.wallet_tx) + extra_inspections.
## Content shapes (A.3):
##   email: time, from_name, from_addr, reply_to, to (you@aegis-solutions.example in the office,
##     you@mymail.example on the phone), subject, body, links
##   sms: time, sender_label, sender_number, sender_info, body, links, optional thread ("kwartapay": the items of
##     one thread render as one conversation, earlier available items as muted bubbles above)
##   chat (Kumusta Chat in the office, ChatLink on the phone): time, sender_label, handle, profile (lines hidden
##     until inspected), body, links, optional request {label, details (hidden until inspected)}
##   An email may carry qrs {<qr id>: url}: drawn as QR codes; "Preview QR link" reveals the url (never opens it).
##   coworker: an email, sms or chat shape plus quote {label, details (hidden until inspected), body}
##   call: caller_id ("LABEL 09XX-XXX-xxxx" form), caller_id_info, caller_name, lines
##   app (kind "app", app "bank": a screen of an app the player opened): time, app_name, app_info (lines hidden
##     until inspected), title, body, links
##   Any message may carry wallet_tx {<tx id>: {dir, amount, value (float), name, number, contact, time, ref}}:
##     shown in KwartaPay History only while its item is unlocked. Tx ids are unique campaign-wide.
##   Body links are [url=<link id>]text[/url]; the real URL is in links[<link id>]. Link ids are unique campaign-wide.
## Step keys (A.4):
##   surface ("desktop" or "call"), question, optional kind ("choices" default or "checklist"), optional task
##   (sub-task label), optional wait_for ("telephone") + wait_objective + trigger_prompt, call_header, call_name,
##   call_lines, optional dial ("8700", "1326" or "2299": the number the keypad must dial; without it the number is
##   read from an "EXT nnnn" call_header), optional checklist_line (the "You" line in the call transcript on a
##   checklist submit; default "(tells Security the warning signs)").
##   choices step: choices = Array of {text, outcome ("correct", "wrong" or "unsafe"), feedback,
##     optional next_step (int; a correct choice without it resolves the item), opens (a Campaign.PAGES id),
##     opens_app (a PHONE_APP_TARGETS id: the phone switches to that app view, applied on correct like opens),
##     shares_secret (true when the choice gives away an OTP or MPIN), response_line,
##     compromise (unsafe only; names Black Veil in the office, a personal loss at home and in the cafe)}.
##   checklist step: submit_text, options (Array of {text, real, why}), feedback (shown on a correct submit).
## Inspection keys (A.5): "sender" (mail), "sender_number" (messages), "caller_id" (calls), "quote" (coworker items),
##   "link:<link id>" (set when the link is pasted in the Browser), "profile" (chat items), "request" (chat items
##   with a request), "qr:<qr id>" (set by Preview QR link; credited to the item that owns the QR code),
##   "app_info" (bank app items), "tx:<tx id>" (a KwartaPay History entry; credited to the item that owns it),
##   "wallet_inbox" (the KwartaPay Inbox tab) and "page:<PAGES id>" (a phone Browser bookmark; both shared: credited
##   to every unlocked item that requires them).
##   QR ids are unique campaign-wide and differ from every item id and link id.

